<title>USA: OEA says Pyrospace merges with Pyromeca.</title>
<headline>OEA says Pyrospace merges with Pyromeca.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>OEA Inc said Wednesday that Pyrospace, its French aerospace affiliate, merged with the French company Pyromeca.</p>
<p>OEA said the new entity will be called PKS, and that OEA will retain a 10 percent ownership in the new company.</p>
<p>OEA's remaining share of Pyrospace will be sold to SNPE, a private French aerospace company, for 25 million French francs, or about US$5 million.</p>
<p>OEA will use the cash proceeds to help fund the rapid growth of Pyroindustrie, its French automotive subsidiary.</p>
</text>
